---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="SPD Training & In-Service Documentation Software | Certivue"
  description="Assign training to your sterile processing team, upload in-service documents, and keep a complete, survey-ready record of every staff education activity."
  canonical="https://certivue.com/training-records"
>
  <section style="padding-top:140px; padding-bottom:64px; padding-left:20px; padding-right:20px;">
    <div style="max-width:760px; margin:0 auto;">
      <h1 style="color:#fff; font-size:clamp(32px, 6vw, 48px); font-weight:500; letter-spacing:-1px; line-height:1.15; margin:0 0 20px;">
        SPD Training &amp; In-Service Documentation Software
      </h1>
      <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:17px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
        Assign training to your sterile processing staff, attach the supporting documents, and keep a complete record of every in-service and education activity — organized, accessible, and ready for survey day.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding:0 20px 80px;">
    <div style="max-width:760px; margin:0 auto; display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:48px;">

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          In-service records shouldn't live in a filing cabinet
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Sterile processing departments run constant training — new instrument sets, updated IFUs, vendor in-services, annual competencies. But when that training is documented on sign-in sheets and paper handouts stuffed in a binder, proving it happened is a scramble. Surveyors want to see who was trained, on what, and when — and paper doesn't answer quickly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          Assign training to your whole team at once
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Create a training record and assign it to multiple staff members in one step, so a department-wide in-service is logged for everyone without duplicating work. Each staff member's record reflects exactly what they've been assigned and completed.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          Keep the documentation attached
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Upload the supporting material — sign-in sheets, handouts, vendor documentation, competency paperwork — directly to the training record. The evidence lives with the record, so when someone asks for proof, it's one click away instead of a hunt through a filing cabinet.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 12px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          A complete education history for every technician
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; margin:0;">
          Every training assignment and completion builds a running education history for each staff member. Instead of reconstructing who attended what, you have a continuous, organized record for the whole department that's ready whenever you need it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div style="text-align:center; background:#161820; border:0.5px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); border-radius:12px; padding:48px;">
        <h2 style="color:#fff; font-size:26px; font-weight:500; margin:0 0 10px; letter-spacing:-0.3px;">
          See training documentation in action
        </h2>
        <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.5); font-size:15px; margin-bottom:28px;">
          Give your SPD team one place to assign, document, and prove every in-service.
        </p>
        <a
          href="/#demo"
          style="display:inline-block; background:#22d3c8; color:#0f1117; font-weight:500; border-radius:8px; padding:10px 22px; text-decoration:none; font-size:15px;"
        >
          Request a demo
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
